parameters.prompt:
INCIDENT COMMANDER - unknown assets - ${trigger.incident_id}

No evidence could be collected from: ${know_scan.artifacts.p2s_unknown_summary}
Unknown is not clear.

APPROVE = open a network-isolation request and assign an owner.
REJECT = record as accepted risk (requires a named owner on the case).

Draft a network-isolation request for the network team for these unknown assets in ${trigger.incident_id} (PHP2Shell): ${know_scan.artifacts.p2s_unknown_summary}. State why (no evidence could be collected; give the inventory exposure exactly as listed), the requested action (block inbound HTTP/HTTPS at the perimeter until an owner verifies the asset), the approver (${escalate_ic.decided_by}) and the review deadline (72 hours). The body is at most 120 words. It is a draft; do not claim anything was sent or isolated. Use only the facts above. End the body with: "Isolation stays in place until an owner verifies the asset."

Return only one JSON object that matches this JSON schema, with no other text before or after it:
{"properties":{"body":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"title":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["title","body"],"type":"object"}

The AI-extracted spec is outside the reviewed envelope: ${contain_gate.artifacts.p2s_spec_violations}
Nothing has been applied. Update the reviewed role through a pull request, then re-run.
APPROVE = acknowledge and assign; REJECT = discard the extraction.

The extracted mitigation spec for ${trigger.incident_id} contains items outside the reviewed control role: ${contain_gate.artifacts.p2s_spec_violations}. Full spec: ${check_contain_extract.artifacts.p2s_ai}. Draft a pull request description for the automation team: what to add to the role's allowed parameter envelope, the advisory citation for each item, the verification check that must be added, and the test that must pass before merge. Do not write the code; the PR is reviewed and merged by humans.

Return only one JSON object that matches this JSON schema, with no other text before or after it:
{"properties":{"body":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"checks_to_add":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"title":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["title","body"],"type":"object"}

CONTAIN - PHP2Shell - ${trigger.incident_id}

${check_know_brief.artifacts.p2s_ai.exec_summary}

Apply interim controls to: ${know_scan.artifacts.p2s_action_services_text}
Controls (AI-extracted from the recorded advisories, inside the reviewed envelope): ${contain_gate.artifacts.p2s_spec_settings}
Prerequisites enforced by automation: php_admin_value scope, cgroup memory boundary, worker restart (not reload).
Pending services from scan: ${know_scan.artifacts.p2s_pending_services}
Isolation for pending services removes HTTP access from other hosts.
Tested commit: ${contain_test.artifacts.p2s_commit}
Test environment: every verification check passed - ${contain_test.job_url}

Residual risk, quoted from the recorded advisory: "${check_contain_extract.artifacts.p2s_ai.residual_risk_quote}"

APPROVE = apply and verify in production, one host at a time.
REJECT = no change; the exposure stays open on the incident.

Write the CONTAIN status update for the CISO and board for ${trigger.incident_id} (PHP2Shell).

Production verification (JSON): ${contain_prod.artifacts.p2s_verify}
Unknown assets (no evidence collected): ${know_scan.artifacts.p2s_unknown_summary}
Services with no fix available: ${know_scan.artifacts.p2s_pending_services}
Log look-back: ${know_lookback.artifacts.p2s_lookback_text}
Residual risk (verbatim sentence from Red Hat bulletin RHSB-2026-013): "${check_contain_extract.artifacts.p2s_ai.residual_risk_quote}"
Approved by security owner: ${approve_security.decided_by} at ${approve_security.decided_at}
Service owner decision: ${approve_service.decision} by ${approve_service.decided_by} at ${approve_service.decided_at}

Rules: report only what the verification shows. "Control verified" is not "safe" - say so. List open items explicitly (vendor appliance waiting for a fix, unknown assets, forensic triage). Name the next decision point. Use only dates and times stated above; never invent a date, deadline or schedule. Do not restate approvals or their times; the workflow keeps the approval record. Forensic triage is recommended, not started: never write that it is in progress or underway. Attribute statements to their source: "Red Hat" for RHSB-2026-013, "PHP" for php.net; use "vendor" only for the AcmeCMS appliance vendor.

Return only one JSON object that matches this JSON schema, with no other text before or after it:
{"properties":{"headline":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"next_decision":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"not_claimed":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"open_items":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"verified":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"required":["headline","verified","not_claimed","open_items","next_decision"],"type":"object"}
